# Project

Electron + React 18 + TypeScript calendar for Windows. Product name is Kip. UI matches Apple Calendar / Fantastical-style layout: three columns, Inter, glass panels, tokens in `src/styles/globals.css` and `tailwind.config.js`.

- Renderer in `src/`. Main, preload, ICS, and CalDAV in `electron/`.
- Import renderer modules with `@/`.
- State is Zustand (`calendarStore`, `eventStore`, `taskStore`, `settingsStore`). Do not add another state library.
- Dates: `date-fns`. Natural language: `chrono-node` through `src/lib/nlpParser.ts`.
- Icons: Lucide. Motion: Framer Motion with `EASE` from `src/lib/constants.ts`.
- No UI kit and no extra drag library. Shared controls live in `src/components/ui`.
- Views read and write store state. Seed data is only the initial store contents.
- Desktop APIs go through `window.api`. The renderer must still render when `window.api` is missing.
- Windows shortcuts use Ctrl: 1–5 switch views, Ctrl+K new event, Ctrl+T today, Ctrl+F search.
- Colors come from `PALETTE`. Event blocks use `eventStyle()`.
- Google and iCloud calendars merge through `mergeRemoteCalendars`. Do not call those APIs from React components.

```tsx
// Good: store action, desktop bridge optional
useEventStore.getState().addEvent(draft)
window.api?.notify({ title, body })
```
